α",16,248],["ἐφίλησεν",1391,3],["αὐτὴν",3,98],["καὶ",2,8],["ἡ",1,11],["ψυχὴ",63,13],["αὐτοῦ",3,48],["ἐκολλήθη",1246,38],["σφόδρα",150,17],["αὐτῇ",3,99],["καὶ",2,8],["ἦλθεν",55,3],["εἰς",8,1],["Ἐκβάτανα",2841,13]],"and the devil shall smell it, and flee away, and never come again any more: but when thou shalt come to her, rise up both of you, and pray to God which is merciful, who will have pity on you, and save you: fear not, for she is appointed unto thee from the beginning; and thou shalt preserve her, and she shall go with thee. Moreover I suppose that she shall bear thee children. Now when Tobias had heard these things, he loved her, and his heart was effectually joined to her. And he came to Ecbatane."]]